The paper’s first decisive split is now clear: unrestricted flow conservation is linear algebra, while Section 3.2 reports NP-completeness for bounded zero-sum flows on \((3,4)\)-graphs (3-flow) and \((2,3)\)-graphs (4-flow), with bipartite graphs explicitly polynomial-time. I’m checking the full theorem text and the existing workspace module before choosing the bounded native family; an unrestricted planted-flow family would fail H.
