+"""Inverse-generated nowhere-zero 3-flows in signed (3,4)-graphs.
+
+The native definitions are from Sections 1 and 2 of arXiv:1608.06944.
+Section 2.7 identifies zero-sum flows with flows in all-negative signed graphs
+and reports NP-completeness for zero-sum 3-flow on (3,4)-graphs.  Instances
+below are assembled from local zero-sum patterns, then carried through random
+edge reorientations and signed-graph switchings.  Thus the certificate is
+known before the public bidirected graph exists; generation never solves the
+instance.
