The prior draft does not survive construction-aware analysis: once the degree-3 sign types are found, the remaining “magnitude-two” choices are exactly a bipartite perfect-matching problem. A two-stage exact-type + Hopcroft–Karp attack solved all 8 shipping seeds in about 0.008–0.030 seconds. That invalidates the Track A claim and G6, so I will not ship the draft as-is. I’m testing a native non-bipartite `(3,4)` inverse construction that removes this matching collapse.
